@page "/components/ai/scrolltolatest"

<PageOutlet Url="components/ai/scrolltolatest"
            Title="AiScrollToLatest"
            Description="BitAiScrollToLatest is the button that appears when the reader has scrolled away from the newest message of an AI transcript, and takes them back to it." />

<DemoPage Name="AiScrollToLatest"
          Description="BitAiScrollToLatest is the floating button that appears when the reader has scrolled away from the newest message of a transcript and takes them back to it. It renders only while Visible - there is somewhere to go - and floats centered above its nearest positioned ancestor, which in a BitAiChat is the footer, so it sits just above the composer whatever height the composer has. Pair it with the OnPinnedChange and ScrollToLatestAsync of a BitAiMessageList."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          CssVariables="componentCssVariables"
          GitHubAIUrl="ScrollToLatest/BitAiScrollToLatest.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="AI/ScrollToLatest/BitAiScrollToLatestDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.AI" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            The button decides nothing on its own: <b>Visible</b> says whether to show it and <b>OnClick</b> what pressing it
            does. <BitLink Href="/components/ai/chat">BitAiChat</BitLink> wires both to its transcript for you; a chat assembled
            by hand wires them to a <BitLink Href="/components/ai/messagelist">BitAiMessageList</BitLink>. It is positioned
            absolutely, so its container needs <b>position: relative</b> (or any other positioning) and room above it.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            The button is a labelled BitButton (the ScrollToLatest string, "Scroll to latest", unless <b>Label</b> says
            otherwise), so it is reachable with the keyboard and named for a screen reader. Once pressed it goes away, as the
            view reaches the newest message, and the focus would go with it to the page: BitAiChat moves it to its composer,
            and a chat assembled by hand does the same in its <b>OnClick</b> (the <b>FocusAsync</b> of a
            <BitLink Href="/components/ai/promptinput">BitAiPromptInput</BitLink>). Its entrance follows the motion tokens and
            is skipped under reduced motion, and it is left out of a printout.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                Nothing is rendered until <b>Visible</b> is set; then the button floats centered above the box it is in, and
                <b>OnClick</b> reports a press.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitToggle @bind-Value="isVisible" Text="Visible" />
            <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri);text-align:center">
                <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible="isVisible" OnClick="HandleClick" />
                The positioned box it floats above, such as the footer of a chat.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>Pressed <b>@clicks</b> times.</div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="With a message list" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                What it is for: the <b>OnPinnedChange</b> of a BitAiMessageList shows it when the reader scrolls up, and its
                <b>ScrollToLatestAsync</b> takes them back. Scroll the transcript up.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="height:400px;display:flex;flex-direction:column">
                <BitAiMessageList @ref="list" Conversation="conversation" OnPinnedChange="HandlePinnedChange" />
                <div style="position:relative;padding:0.75rem;text-align:center;color:var(--bit-clr-fg-ter)">
                    <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible="@(isPinned is false)" OnClick="ScrollToLatest" />
                    The footer of the transcript.
                </div>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Label" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                <b>Label</b> words the button in place of the string table's "Scroll to latest" - to say there are new
                messages, for instance.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible Label="3 new messages" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                A disabled button is shown but takes no press.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible Disabled />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                <b>BitParams</b> with a <b>BitAiScrollToLatestParams</b> sets the label, the classes and the styles of every
                button inside it; a button's own value wins. Whether it is shown and what pressing it does are not cascaded. The
                label reaches the button of each BitAiChat in it too, while its classes and styles come from the chat's own
                <b>Styles</b> / <b>Classes</b> (their <b>ScrollToLatest</b> member).
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitParams Parameters="scrollParams">
                <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                    <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible />
                </div>
                <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                    <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible Label="Its own label wins" />
                </div>
            </BitParams>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> / <b>Class</b> reach the root, <b>Styles</b> / <b>Classes</b> its <b>Button</b> (the class-styles
                of BitButton). The public <b>--bit-AiScrollToLatest-*</b> variables (see the CSS variables table) move it and
                lift it from <b>:root</b>, an ancestor or <b>Style</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>
                <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                    <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible
                                         Style="box-shadow:none"
                                         Styles="@(new() { Button = new() { Root = "background:linear-gradient(90deg, #7c3aed, #2563eb);color:#fff;border:none" } })" />
                </div>
                <div style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                    <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible
                                         Class="custom-scroll"
                                         Classes="@(new() { Button = new() { Root = "custom-scroll-button" } })" />
                </div>
                <div style="position:relative;margin-top:5rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                    <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible
                                         Style="--bit-AiScrollToLatest-offset:1.5rem;--bit-AiScrollToLatest-shadow:0 0 0 0.25rem var(--bit-clr-pri-tint);--bit-AiScrollToLatest-z-index:10" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" Id="example7">
            <div>Use BitAiScrollToLatest in right-to-left (RTL).</div>
            <br />
            <div dir="rtl" style="position:relative;margin-top:4rem;padding:1rem;border:1px dashed var(--bit-clr-brd-pri)">
                <BitAiScrollToLatest Visible Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Label="رفتن به آخرین پیام" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
